<title>CANADA: Slocan &quot;interested in good acquisitions&quot;.</title>
<headline>Slocan &quot;interested in good acquisitions&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slocan Forest Products Ltd, when asked whether it might want to acquire TimberWest Forest Ltd, said on Friday that it was interested in making good acquisitions.</p>
<p>&quot;We're always interested in good acquisitions. We're buyers, not sellers, and that's all I can say for now,&quot; said Slocan Chief Executive Ike Barber.</p>
<p>TimberWest said earlier that it and its 52 percent owner Fletcher Challenge Canada Ltd would seek to find a buyer for TimberWest. Fletcher Canada is majority owned by New Zealand's Fletcher Challenge Ltd.</p>
<p>Analysts speculated Slocan might be among the forest companies interested in TimberWest.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314</p>
</text>
